{
  "abstract": "Can a multi-layer causal Transformer be trained without a backward pass—executing zero reverse pullbacks, zero VJP helpers, and zero same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while improving speed and short-horizon accuracy over matched-routing node-perturbation baselines? We study a 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) pipeline across 84 backward-free multi-seed arms (exp26–exp42, plus 7 local-pullback and 2 exact-backpropagation references) on ClimbMix d6 (L=6, D in {256, 384, 512, 768}, 360–720 steps) and Native 50.3M (L=8, D=512, T=2,048, 100 steps). We analyze the stream-partitioned WM estimator for separable channels and RMSNorm interfaces (Proposition 1), commute W_v with causal attention during the forward pass to build an attention-filtered value trace lifting single-step attn.c_v cosine alignment 8.2x (+0.1104 -> +0.9069, Proposition 2), route lexical credit via a diagonal skip surrogate (Proposition 3), and bound the expected same-token RMSNorm post-installation residual by kappa_4(x)/D (Proposition 4), verified across a 16-cell factorial and compliant pure-FP32 controls (2.1359 vs. 2.1579 BPB). Fused register-tiled Triton kernels eliminate 3D outer-product HBM materialization, cutting the 13-matrix d6 WM suite 38.4x (134.31 -> 3.50 ms/step) and step time 8.33x (155.6 -> 18.68 ms/step; 2.75x on Native 50.3M, 8.07 -> 2.94 s/step). Co-designing Pre-Polar Muon with scale-matched sparse embedding velocity and drift annealing (9.82x Layer-0 / 1.42x 6-layer attention shift) reaches 2.0682 +- 0.0006 DEV BPB on 360-step d6 (within 0.0150 BPB of matched-subset Exact Backpropagation, 2.0532 +- 0.0008), outperforming Surrogate-Routed Local Node Perturbation (SR-LNP) and 76-draw Suffix-Recomputed Node Perturbation (SR-NP, 2.2415 +- 0.0015).",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Resolved all 4 points from the review of PCiFn94K0Wnga54u (paper5_v4_review_report.md): (a) Withdrew all claims of head-to-head superiority over published Dust [9], explicitly renamed train_dust_d6_fast (exp37-exp39) to Surrogate-Routed Local Node Perturbation (SR-LNP) to reflect its terminal-skip routing and gamma=0 local attention scoring, and added a 3-seed Suffix-Recomputed Node Perturbation (SR-NP, exp42_faithful_dust_results.json) control on the matched 4-matrix d6 subset implementing Gaussian perturbations, draw-mean centering, exact suffix recomputation from block l onward, Eq. (4) per-head attention-output alignment, and Eq. (1) future-token accumulation with gamma=0.98 (verified by unit check r_1 = 0.98 * c_2 = 1.47, reaching 2.4264 +- 0.0088 under Adam in 84.38s and 2.2415 +- 0.0015 under Pre-Polar Muon in 65.19s); (b) Replaced the FP32 trace-cache clock controls with compliant zero-pullback Triton WM runs (exp42_fp32_triton_results.json, reverse_error_matmuls_per_step = 0: 2.1359 +- 0.0022 vs. 2.1579 +- 0.0004 at b05, 1e-8 and 2.1274 +- 0.0002 at b09, 1e-4) and explicitly labeled exp36's s_lm @ W_lm runs as local-pullback diagnostic controls (Rev. Matmuls = 1), excluding them from the backward-free count; (c) Included both benchmark_uncontended_timings.json and probe_synthesis_results.json in the supplement, reported both measured 3-seed training GPU times (total_train_gpu_s_mean) and 30-step steady-state benchmark estimates (est_360step_s) in Tables 4-6, and stated the Native 50.3M speedup strictly against the uncontended exp32 reference (8.07s -> 2.94 s/step = 2.75x step speedup, 6.43s -> 1.59s = 4.04x rule speedup); and (d) Regenerated all per-seed table entries directly from the retained JSON records (verified in verify_paper5.py), reported the exact 6-layer mean attention-map shift (0.6046 -> 0.8587 = 1.42x mean across 6 layers, 9.82x in Layer 0), described Pre-Polar Muon accurately as orthogonalizing update directions (presenting the 51.4x higher receiver stable rank as a descriptive association), and reported our controlled 3-seed test of 1/sqrt(BT) embedding scaling on Native 50.3M (exp41: 2.0252 +- 0.0003 at lr_wte=0.015 vs. 1.9845 +- 0.0003 at lr_wte=0.10 and 1.9361 +- 0.0004 in exp32).",
